# Optional overrides. Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment what you need.

# The chat endpoint five of the six angles are generated from (any OpenAI-compatible one).
# SKILLS_PROFILES_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
# SKILLS_PROFILES_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com/v1
# SKILLS_PROFILES_API_KEY=sk-...

# Extra attempts per LLM call; a 429 or a 5xx is retried with backoff. 0 = a single try.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_MAX_RETRIES=3

# Seconds per request. The SDK's own default is ten minutes, which parks a worker on a
# connection that is never coming back; every call here finishes in well under one.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_TIMEOUT=120

# Let the model reason before it answers. This is a provider extension rather than an
# OpenAI field, spelled the way Agnes documents it - `chat_template_kwargs` with
# `enable_thinking` - so leave it off for an endpoint that will not accept the field.
# The reasoning comes back in a `reasoning_content` nothing here reads; the answer still
# arrives as strict json. Costs a few hundred extra output tokens per profile.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_THINKING=1

# Fake LLM, real layout: the same thing `just dry=1` sets. No API calls, no key needed.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_DRY_RUN=1

# The second endpoint, for the angles `jev.py` names: Jev (TypeSafe System One) over 302.AI. It is
# not OpenAI-compatible, and its answers are typed rather than written, so it has settings of its own.
# The provider's own namespace: 302.AI's generic /v1 gateway has no channel for it.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_JEV_API_KEY=sk-...
# SKILLS_PROFILES_JEV_BASE_URL=https://api.302.ai/typesafeai/v1/systemone
# SKILLS_PROFILES_JEV_MODEL=jev-latest

# Seconds per System One request, and the retries after one. The endpoint is fast, and drops the
# first call after it has been idle - which arrives as a timeout and is what the retries are for.
# SKILLS_PROFILES_JEV_TIMEOUT=20
# SKILLS_PROFILES_JEV_MAX_RETRIES=3

# Everything this file can set is the scripts' own: the two endpoints, their keys and models, and the
# dry-run switch. The paths and the batch knobs are `just` variables instead - `just output_dir=/tmp/x`,
# `just limit=20 jobs=8 rpm=20` - so nothing here can silently change where a batch reads or writes.
